# Rule 2 — Continuous until applied + skipped = 30

**Session ceiling:** Keep going until `applied + skipped >= 30` (or results are truly exhausted).

- Apply Naukri **All Filters once** per search, then run continuously — **never** ask the user to click Next page or Apply more mid-run.
- Flow: **filters → scan (auto next-page) → apply queued matches → continue** until `applied + skipped >= 30`.
  - Do not end a session while matched jobs are still **Queued**.
  - Cap `betweenJobs` (~0.6–1.2s). Skip read pauses and the 2-minute session break during the batch.
  - Navigate **job → next job** — do not return to the search list between applies.
  - If pages/searches exhaust with `0 < processed < 30`, stop after applying every match found — do not block on a full 30.
  - If nothing matched, do not apply; report that nothing matched.
- Show **Apply more** / **Close — view dashboard** only when the session is actually finished (hit 30 or exhausted). Close must close the Naukri work tab and open the Cosmo dashboard (reuse an existing Cosmo tab when possible).
- Never invent extra result pages past real pagination.
- Single Naukri work tab only.
